nalty loop (150 metres) skied for each missed target."]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Course Length: 9,813 m" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 37 m" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 38 m" [:br {}] "Shooting 1: Prone at 3.159 km, 50 m range" [:br {}] "Shooting 2: Standing at 6.583 km, 50 m range" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 348 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The men’s 10 km sprint biathlon competition of the PyeongChang 2018 Olympics was held on 11 February 2018 at the Alpensia Biathlon Centre. The event was won surprisingly by German " [:a {:href "/athletes/118509"} "Arnd Peiffer"] ", with Czech " [:a {:href "/athletes/127594"} "Michal Krčmář"] " taking silver and Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/127920"} "Dominik Windisch"] " bronze. Both Peiffer and Krčmář hit all their targets, the same as " [:a {:href "/athletes/137097"} "Olli Hiidensalo"] " from Finland and Ukraine " [:a {:href "/athletes/128647"} "Dmytro Pidruchniy"] ", who finished 19th and 21st, respectively. Favored " [:a {:href "/athletes/118554"} "Martin Fourcade"] " from France missed three targets and came in a disappointing eighth. Even worse was Norwegian star " [:a {:href "/athletes/128188"} "Johannes Thingnes Bø"] ", who missed four targets and finishing 31st. The competition was influenced by heavy winds and very cold weather with a temperature around -12º C."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Misses"] [:th {} "Shooting 1 Misses"] [:th {} "Shooting 1"] [:th {} "Shooting 2 Misses"] [:th {} "Shooting 2"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/118509"} "Arnd Peiffer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "23:38.8"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "8:01.8 (14